cifs: avoid dup prefix path in dfs_get_automount_devname()

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10
commit-author Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.com>
commit d5a863a153e90996ab2aef6b9e08d509f4d5662b
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10/d5a863a1.failed

@server->origin_fullpath already contains the tree name + optional
prefix, so avoid calling __build_path_from_dentry_optional_prefix() as
it might end up duplicating prefix path from @cifs_sb->prepath into
final full path.

Instead, generate DFS full path by simply merging
@server->origin_fullpath with dentry's path.

This fixes the following case

	mount.cifs //root/dfs/dir /mnt/ -o ...
	ls /mnt/link

where cifs_dfs_do_automount() will call smb3_parse_devname() with
@devname set to "//root/dfs/dir/link" instead of
"//root/dfs/dir/dir/link".

Fixes: 7ad54b98fc1f ("cifs: use origin fullpath for automounts")
	Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org> # 6.2+
	Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara (SUSE) <pc@manguebit.com>
	Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit d5a863a153e90996ab2aef6b9e08d509f4d5662b)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/cifs/dfs.h
* Unmerged path fs/cifs/dfs.h
diff --git a/fs/cifs/cifs_dfs_ref.c b/fs/cifs/cifs_dfs_ref.c
index e0edfc02f320..3481469e8386 100644
--- a/fs/cifs/cifs_dfs_ref.c
+++ b/fs/cifs/cifs_dfs_ref.c
@@ -289,8 +289,6 @@ static struct vfsmount *cifs_dfs_do_automount(struct path *path)
 		mnt = ERR_CAST(full_path);
 		goto out;
 	}
-
-	convert_delimiter(full_path, '/');
 	cifs_dbg(FYI, "%s: full_path: %s\n", __func__, full_path);
 
 	tmp = *cur_ctx;
* Unmerged path fs/cifs/dfs.h
